    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, with every derived value following from it.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1`** (`rest/controller/v1/`)\n- Replaced the sequence-based `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` with `customerCodeFor(Owner)`, which builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n  - **REGION** \u2014 derived from the postcode via `ownerMapper.regionOf(owner)` (postcode range \u2192 city table \u2192 `UNKNOWN`).\n  - **HASH8** \u2014 first 8 upper-case hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)` (telephone is already normalized to E.164 by the time the code is built).\n- Added the `sha256UpperHex` helper (and the `MessageDigest`/`StandardCharsets`/`NoSuchAlgorithmException` imports).\n- The sequence number is dropped entirely. The membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), its Luhn check digit (over the digits in the code), and the create-audit line all read from `customerCode`, so they automatically move to the new identity \u2014 the audit now logs e.g. `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`** (`mapper/`)\n- `toLocality` now takes the region from the `<REGION>` segment of the `customerCode` (everything before the first `-`), so locality moves with the new identity. It falls back to `regionOf(owner)` for legacy records with no code (which reproduces the previous `UNKNOWN` result for the unmapped seed cities).\n- Extracted the old postcode-preferred region logic into the reusable `regionOf(Owner)` used both when building the code and as the locality fallback.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` field descriptions and examples to document the region-and-hash scheme (these regenerate the DTOs but don't change field structure).\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: the spec says REGION is \"derived from the postcode,\" but owners can lack a postcode, so I reused the existing postcode-preferred-then-city-then-`UNKNOWN` derivation rather than postcode-only \u2014 this keeps locality consistent with prior behavior for known cities and never yields an empty region segment.",
